# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each machine's
# `core.autocrlf`, because this project has already lost data to them twice.
#
# The first time was the upstream cache: a `git clone` on Windows produced CRLF,
# regexes anchored with `$` stopped matching without erroring, and a sync
# produced a materially smaller knowledge base than the same commit synced on
# Linux. That is fixed at the read boundary in `src/parse/util.ts`.
#
# The second is this repository's own tree, and it is why this file exists. The
# rendered Markdown is committed and CI re-renders it to prove the output is
# reproducible from `data/`. With no attributes, a fresh clone on a machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out as CRLF, the renderer writes LF, and
# every one of the 160 generated pages reads as modified.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Two exceptions, and they are the point of a test rather than an oversight.
# `test/parse.test.ts` asserts the parser survives a CRLF checkout. Both
# fixtures are stored LF in the index, so on any machine that checks out LF —
# every Linux CI runner — that test passed without testing anything. These two
# must arrive CRLF in the working tree for it to mean what it says.
test/fixtures/cache/zeppos-docs/docs/reference/related-resources/device-list.mdx eol=crlf
test/fixtures/cache/zeppos-docs/static/llms/@zos-interaction.md eol=crlf

